  "summary": "Base64 decoding patterns in bundled CLI without corroborating exfiltration evidence",
  "details": "The package's bundled CLI files (dist/cli.cjs and dist/cli.js) contain Buffer.from(..., 'base64').toString(...) patterns at multiple locations. Base64 decoding is a common primitive in bundled JavaScript for handling inline assets, encoded configuration, JWT parsing, or ordinary string handling in build output, and no traced code path shows the decoded content being executed, nor any hardcoded exfiltration endpoint, credential read, or lifecycle-hook execution. The keyword co-occurrence in a minified bundle is insufficient on its own to establish malicious intent.",
